module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness that fails to COMPILE is ABSENT rather than red, and running its SUBJECT proves nothing about it** (a claim file is committed, reviewed and merged while it cannot compile, so none of its assertions ever execute and the guarantee it was written to carry does not exist; the class it polices reports as walled while nothing walls it, which is worse than an absent witness because the file is cited as coverage by its own author and by its reviewers). ",
    "WHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT A SLIP: every ordinary signal is compatible with the dead file and NONE OF THEM IS MALFUNCTIONING. It emits no advisories, because a file that does not compile contributes none. It fails no assertions, because none run. It is ABSENT from the floor disposition rather than failing in it, so a disposition read shows nothing to investigate. `cargo fmt` is green because the file is well-formed text. The push is green. And a reviewer can APPROVE on a wholly correct reading of the source, because READING DOES NOT COMPILE. ",
    "THE CORE IS A TWO-CLAIM COLLAPSE: `the compiler behaves correctly` and `the witness that enrols that behaviour as executing evidence works` are DIFFERENT CLAIMS, and running the subject as a direct fixture establishes only the first. The mechanism of the misread is that holding the stronger claim's output makes the weaker one feel already answered — the author has the passing fixtures in hand, which is exactly why the file meant to carry them never gets checked. ",
    "RECOGNITION RULE: ask what would have caught it, and IF THE ONLY ANSWER IS A RUN AIMED AT A DIFFERENT QUESTION, the class has no dedicated detector. The specimen surfaced from a whole-tree advisory census re-derivation chasing an unrelated hypothesis about a denominator, as blocking error number one, after the arms were green, the PR was open and an APPROVE was already recorded. THE ONE INSTRUMENT THAT SEES IT is a whole-tree compile INCLUDING the test roots; compiling the subject, or entry-scoping to the witness itself, does not. ",
    "Rung found at 1, mitigatable, held only by an unrelated run happening to range over the file, which is not a mechanism. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: the population is decidable and closed — every file under the claim roots — so a required step that compiles them and refuses a non-compiling claim file makes the state unwritable in an `Accepted` tree. NEXT TRIGGER, capability and not artifact: the required floor must COMPILE every claim-root file and refuse a claim file that does not compile, rather than only executing the claim files that compile — AN EXECUTION ROSTER KEYED TO COMPILING FILES CANNOT SEE A FILE THAT FELL OUT OF IT, the same shape as a check whose population IS its own roster. Specimen gunbc#10337: `brand_nominal_identity_witness_test` named a host builtin in its import list; four direct fixtures had already proven the compiler refuses, and the witness enrolling them had never run. ",
    "THE TRIGGER'S GRAIN IS NARROWER THAN THE RULED CAPABILITY, AND THIS RECEIPT WIDENS IT RATHER THAN LETTING THE NARROW TEXT STAND (sunny-tern-813 ruling, relayed and verified by crisp-lynx-452, 2026-09-11; filed from the joint-incompatibility scope, gunbc.plans.joint_incompatibility_claim_join section 2.3). The row above names the capability as `COMPILE every claim-root file`. The ruled capability is WIDER: compile every CONSTRUCTION SITE of a type whose required fields changed, AND every claim-root file regardless of gate closure -- and a construction site can live in a module that is not a claim root at all. DESIGN section 4b(3): a trigger naming less than the capability it restores will be satisfied while the capability stays dead, and the review tell is a grain mismatch between the loss sentence and the trigger sentence. The loss sentence of the second specimen is construction-site grain (`every construction site of that type in the tree`); the trigger sentence is claim-root-file grain. THAT IS THE MISMATCH. So the trigger, as of this receipt, reads at the ruled width: THE REQUIRED FLOOR MUST COMPILE EVERY CLAIM-ROOT FILE AND EVERY CONSTRUCTION SITE OF A TYPE WHOSE DECLARED FIELD SET CHANGED BETWEEN BASE AND HEAD, REGARDLESS OF GATE CLOSURE, AND REFUSE ANY THAT DOES NOT COMPILE. Discharging the narrower sentence alone does not retire this row. ",
    "WHAT THE JOINT-INCOMPATIBILITY SCOPE ESTABLISHED ABOUT THIS ROW, so the two are not conflated: the cross-change join over the declaration index (v1_compiler.bin.joint_claim_join) keys on a module's EXPORT SURFACE -- declared, variants, reexported -- and a field is not a surface entry, so that join is silent on every specimen of this row by construction; the two classes share a shape (a change compiled against a population its diff does not name) and not a mechanism. The within-tree half needs no open-PR set and no cross-change anything: the removed side is `decl_fields` base-minus-head per declaration, derivable from the same base reconstruction the wave wall performs, and the claiming side needs no precise construction-site channel because the COMPILE is the oracle and the index only selects what to compile -- every module whose `referenced` or `authored_type_references` names the changed declaration, where over-collection costs compile time and never a false finding. That is the selection this row's widened trigger names, and it is this row's to discharge, not a checkpoint of the join's plan. THE BOUNDARY OF THAT TRIGGER, STATED SO THE WORD POPULATION IS NOT LATER READ AS MORE THAN IT SAYS: the population compile establishes COMPILABILITY of the claim-root population and NOT EVALUATION of it. A claim file that compiles and whose `test fn`s are declared but absent from the entry's conjunction sails through that wall untouched (cool-badger-34, 2026-09-11: four such fns in a witness module type-checked, read as coverage, were never evaluated, and turned the suite red when enrolled). That second hole -- compiles YES, evaluated NO -- is owned by the neighbour row gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled, whose detector counts constructed fixtures against enrolled assertions; it is not this row's and this trigger does not close it. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
